  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale  \n   **Central Idea**: Use a physics-inspired simulation with adaptive mutation to escape local optima. The solution will evolve piecewise constant functions over [0,2], balancing high-resolution regions with periodic patterns. The mutation mechanism will prioritize phase shifts of hand-crafted solutions to improve diversity.  \n\n   **Key Rationale**:  \n   - Membrane simulation avoids gradient descent pitfalls by randomizing phase-space perturbations.  \n   - Multi-scale structure complements existing 0.381 iterations by introducing harmonic components from Fourier modes.  \n   - **Crucial Bottleneck**: Overrides all local repairs and manually crafted variations. Focuses entirely on continuous improvement of the parent structure.  \n\n   Guidance: Use this as a mathematical compass, not dogma. Surface tension effects (mutations) can be dialed back if stability degrades. Prefer jittered intervals in phase-space over uniform perturbations.\n\n2. Mathematical Specifications  \n   **Variables**: Piecewise constants approximating h(x) via n equally spaced nodes in [0,2]  \n   **Objective**: Minimize C5(h) = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx  \n   **Constraints**:  \n      0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1, \u03a3h_i \u2248 n/2 (exactly n/2 in optimal case)  \n\n   **Representation**: h is a vector of size n (discretization level)  \n   **Solver Use**:\n     - n=96: SLSQP (local refinement)\n     - n=128/192: Small-scale DE + Large-scale Annealed PSO  \n     - n=256+: Hierarchical covariance matrix adaptation  \n\n   **Repair via Projections**:  \n      ProjectCandidate(h, n) =  \n         While invalid:  \n            Clip h = max(0, min(1, h))  \n            Rescale h = h + (target_sum - sum(h)) / n  \n            Tighten h_clipped = Clip h_again  \n            Mark failure if |target_sum - sum(h_clipped)| > 1e-10  \n\n3. Implementation Procedure  \n   **Stage 1: Environment Setup**:  \n      - Input validation/mother configuration  \n      - Compute dx = 2/n, target_sum = n/2  \n      ParentSolution(initial) -> Ensure feasible with tight projection  \n\n   **Stage 2: Solution Assembly**:  \n      z = np.array(initial_h_values)  \n      MutationPattern(n):  \n         Create three templates:  \n            BaseWave = [0.5 + 0.4 * cos(2\u2022pi\u2022t/n + phase) for t in range(n)] + adjustments  \n            SemiCircle = [0.5 + 0.5\u2022erf((t-0.5)\u20222/n-\u03c3) for t in range(n)]  \n            SpikeTrain = [0.9 if abs(t/n - 0.3) < 0.05 else 0.1 for t in range(n)]  \n\n      Project solution meeting constraints  \n\n   **Stage 3: PSO-DE Optimization**:  \n      Initialize VelocityDamp(strength=0.6, time_scale=20)  \n      GlobalTunable({  \n          phase_shifter: Small [0.002, 0.005] increment range,  \n          amplitude: Clamped Scaling [0.9, 1.1]  \n      })  \n\n      while time < budget/4:  \n         For each candidate:  \n            Shift phases uniformly in [0, 2\u2022pi]  \n            Apply rolling vibrations (Gaussian jitter @ rate min(0.1, 1/time))  \n            Trim invalid solutions via Recursive Repair  \n\n         score = get_MembraneStability(candidate)  // Local PID feedback on constraint satisfaction\n\n         if improved global_min:  \n            UpdateBestCandidateWithHistory()  \n\n      Hierarchical upgrades: 2D FFT-convolved Gaussian blur for higher modes  \n\n4. Search Choices & Variations  \n   **Default Setting**:  \n      templates = [SquarePulse, SincKernel, Binary]  // Two 2D modes delayable  \n      verbs: [\n          PhaseShuffle(exponent=2.7),  # Nominally 4.3 but user-tunable\n          AmplitudeWarper(factor=1.5)   # Generates hypersingular interactions necessary for maximum constraint violation\n      ]  \n\n      AdaptiveCMA(strategy='best/1/exp', F=0.92, Cr=0.8)  \n      **Gateways**:\n          1. If stuck: Activate Particle Pheromones (exponentially decaying niche memory)  \n          2. Above threshold: Co-evolve Lagged Regressions (use past optima to warm-start new modes)  \n          3. Time-critical: WavelengthCompression(70%, safety_margin=0.8)  \n\n5. Compute Budget & Robustness  \n   **Dominant Cost**: Lag correlations on length L=2n-1 (O(n^2), but FFT-convected)  \n   **Estimation**:  \n     n=96 -> 4M operations, \u224890s  \n     n=128->9M op, 120s  \n     n=192->16M op, 150s  \n     n=256->27M op, 180s  \n\n   Budget allocation: 60% to repair/PSO, 30% to large- n jumps, 10% validation.  \n\n   **Recovery**:\n      NaN: Repair through envelope scaling  \n      Fitness explosion: Apply adaptive \u03c3 control (\u03c3\u2098\u1d62\u2099=0.2, decay_factor=0.98/dimension)  \n      Kill stuck populations: GeneticDrop(0.5) + small_template_inject  // 75% probability cycle  \n      Wall clock: Each n runs under max budget= 5\u2022n/Macdime\n\n6. Validation and Contract  \n   A: Verify h[feasible region] has 0\u2264h\u22641 +1e-6  \n   B: Score = exact_min_overlap(h)  # authoritative computation  \n   C: roll_forward() on noisy initialization for 1e-2 failures  \n   D: Redundant computation on .01 subset if bound improves  \n   E: Structure: (h, bound, n) tuple matched to Erd\u0151s validator immediately",
